      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18a5cfb8_9679f196",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-11T02:59:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. That\u0027s the goal. But there are several obstacles to get there, which I will fix incrementally.\n\nNot setting the sdk_version property has its own meaning. It means you are given access to all private symbols (i.e. not using SDK/NDK). If sdk_version defaults to min_sdk_version where an empty value has a different meaning (the current in-development version), then a module with an empty sdk_version suddenly lose access to the symbols.\n\nIn addition, the 30+ modules that are setting sdk_version to a value be fixed to use min_sdk_version instead. I will land this first, fix those 30+ modules and then finally make sdk_version to default to min_sdk_version.",
      "parentUuid": "3c785f00_e7d57445",
